WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:08.069
Speaker 1: Tonight, Joe Biden will be delivering
his first joint address, his first address

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:10.820
to a joint session of the House and Senate.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.789
But it's not called the State of the Union
address.

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:17.539
Often in a president's first year, the State
of the Union is just not called the State

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:18.539
of the Union.

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:21.940
And sometimes it's not in February or January.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.340
It's coming in April.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:29.779
And we will be live tonight on YouTube, Twitter
and Facebook with Joe Biden's first address

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:31.660
to a joint session of the House and Senate.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:37.620
We now have learned that tonight Joe Biden
will propose a one point eight trillion dollar

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:46.150
plan, which will include national paid family
leave, universal pre-K, free community college,

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.910
subsidized child care and a whole bunch of
other things.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.330
Now, will it pass as proposed tonight?

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.520
Of course not.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.520
Of course not.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.520
It never does.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.520
That's the same with every president.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.710
This is the starting point.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.280
But Joe Biden will be introducing his American
families plan tonight.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.100
It is part two of the so-called build back
better economic agenda.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.600
There's the two trillion roughly infrastructure
and jobs plan that was released earlier this

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.600
month.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.400
This is now going to be the next piece of
it, a one point eight dollars billion package.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.820
It is being called a generational investment
in the future.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.480
It is billed as something that will help us
compete with China.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.090
It will transform the US economy, and it includes
one trillion dollars in spending over the

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:34.080
next 10 years and an additional eight hundred
billion, which would be targeted tax credits

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.110
for middle class families.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:43.780
The proposal also includes cracking down on
tax loopholes used by high income tax filers.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.950
Joe Biden wants to nearly double the capital
gains rate from 20 to nearly 40 percent for

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.300
households making over a million dollars a
year.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.040
I don't think that's going to happen, but
it's nice that he's proposing it.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.740
Two hundred and twenty five billion dollars
for national paid leave, another two.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.530
Twenty five billion for child care.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.700
And of course, Republicans have already been
criticizing it.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.979
They will be against it in their rebuttal
tonight to Joe Biden's speech.

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:09.700
They will come out against it.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.840
What's my thought about this?

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.939
I think that it is a very reasonable initial
framework.

00:02:14.939 --> 00:02:18.299
We've talked before about, oh, but how will
we pay for it?

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:21.249
First of all, that's never asked about how
do we buy missiles.

00:02:21.249 --> 00:02:23.269
It's never asked about how we pay for war.

00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:26.040
It's never asked about how we pay for tax
cuts for the rich.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:33.870
It's asked by Republicans when it's actual
programs that they believe are either wasteful

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:39.160
or that go to people who are undeserving in
some way under this umbrella of the morality

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.510
that they apply to.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.730
Who deserves something from the government.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.939
Of course, they're going to be against it.

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:48.620
Our new framework for understanding debt and
deficit.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:56.340
Is that not every dollar of debt is created
equal if we take on a dollar of debt to give

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:02.280
a really rich person a tax break, statistically
most of that money they save just sits in

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.060
a bank account with a relatively low economic
multiplier.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.559
If we accrue a dollar of debt in order to
give somebody a better education, which allows

00:03:11.559 --> 00:03:16.579
them to earn more later in life, paying more
taxes into the government, or if we take on

00:03:16.579 --> 00:03:21.409
a dollar of debt to give someone health care
that doesn't otherwise have it, so that now

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:27.499
they can get a preemptive treatment, preventive
treatment, rather than going to the doctor

00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:29.510
when they are already sick.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.999
And then they miss fewer days of work and
earn higher wages.

00:03:32.999 --> 00:03:38.299
You understand how there are stimulative reasons
for the government to deficit spend and less

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:41.069
or non stimulative reasons?

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:46.650
The framework here is that most of this stuff
would have a higher economic multiplier than

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.159
just tax cuts for the rich.

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:51.030
Now, do I think that this is going to pass
as proposed?

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:57.449
There's no way in hell, there's no way in
hell, because even Democrats are not unanimously

00:03:57.449 --> 00:04:02.329
on board here with the things that Joe Biden
is going to be proposing.

00:04:02.329 --> 00:04:09.269
So I think that Joe Biden is very well positioned
right now with the success of vaccination,

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:12.370
the passage of the one point nine dollars
billion covid stimulus.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.719
Joe Biden has a lot of political capital right
now.

00:04:15.719 --> 00:04:19.049
We've been wondering how is he going to choose
to spend it?

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:23.120
And it is going to be on this two trillion
plus now, one point eight dollars billion

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.120
package.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.569
Now, the the I am not looking for I think
I'm committing.

00:04:28.569 --> 00:04:29.569
We'll see.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:35.759
I think I'm committing not to deal with the
really predictable right wing opposition,

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:38.690
which is where are we going to get this four
trillion dollars?

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.060
It's just like I'm tired of it.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.060
I'm tired of it.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.710
I've done deep dives on exactly where we can
cut spending.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:50.340
I've explained modern monetary theory and
the reality about how a country's debt is

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.620
not the same as a household that we've done
it all.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:57.940
So if they're going to just come out and say
we just we don't have the four trillion and

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.070
we can't keep printing money, I'm so tired
of that.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.520
Maybe I'll address it in passing, but I'm
not going to address that in detail.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.100
I'm more interested.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:14.449
And hearing from Republicans good faith critiques
of why the spending specifically is not a

00:05:14.449 --> 00:05:18.720
good investment in the future of America,
like actually tell me, OK, he wants to do

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.050
free tuition on community college.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.159
Why is that bad?

00:05:22.159 --> 00:05:28.039
It seems to me that it is, number one, a great
alternative for four year to four year schools

00:05:28.039 --> 00:05:30.610
for people for whom maybe that's not the best
fit.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:35.389
It is a great feeder to reduce the total costs
for people who ultimately do want to go to

00:05:35.389 --> 00:05:39.629
a four year school and earn a bachelor's degree,
it seems economically stimulative.

00:05:39.629 --> 00:05:41.450
It will make us more competitive.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.919
Tell me why it's a bad idea to spend money
on that rather than just throwing at me?

00:05:44.919 --> 00:05:47.370
Well, for four trillion, whereas Biden getting
it.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.530
Come on, that's pathetic.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:49.730
That's flaccid.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.610
It's a very flimsy criticism.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:58.409
So I'm hoping to engage more substantively
with criticisms that are made in good faith

00:05:58.409 --> 00:06:01.620
and that are not just the same old thing we've
heard time and time again.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:02.620
That's tonight.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:03.729
Joe Biden will announce it.

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:09.400
I will be live starting at 8:00 p.m. Eastern
on YouTube, Twitch and Facebook.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:46.129
And I hope you'll join me for 

00:06:46.129 --> 00:07:09.500
that speech tonight.

